<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caterino Zeno</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caterino Zeno was a Venetian merchant and diplomat sent in 1471 as ambassador to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a>, whose wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodora-megale-komnene">Despina Khatun</a> was the aunt of Zeno's wife. He worked for an alliance between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and Uzun Hasan against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and travelled to European courts to seek support for it. An account of his travels was published by his descendants in the sixteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caterino-zeno.jpg" alt="Caterino Zeno" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abxbay · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zen_arms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
